signee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible from 9fe0b53081e79d8d739882cdc49d39fdaec12b80, not any released version.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev.double (9fe0b5308) - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:41:30 +0000 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors (2560x1440 @ 59.95 Hz, 2560x1440 @ 59.95 Hz) - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 (nvidia; 615.71.09) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 154.8 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen creating a built-in node type in the scene tree, the node name casing has no effect.\n\nI am quite sure this is due to the recently-merged https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123637.\n\nWhen creating nodes with script types, creating a _new scene_ rather than adding a node to an existing scene, or reverting a node to its \"default\" name by trying to set it to the empty string, the node name casing setting is applied as expected. These processes follow a different code path.\n\nIt's possible that the fix in PR 123637 was incomplete because it won't have applied to all cases where nodes are named. I haven't looked into that.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nIn a project, configured a node name casing setting other than PascalCase. I use snake_case. Add a _built-in_ node type, such as Node3D. It will be named Node3D.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[name-casing_2026-09-28_01-17-10.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32713496/name-casing_2026-09-28_01-17-10.zip)\n\nThis project is configured with snake_case naming. Add a built-in node to a scene via the scene tree and it will not be snake_case named.","closed_by":{"login":"Re